<div class="secret" role="status">
  <p class="notice notice-info" data-invitation-saved><strong>The invitation is saved.</strong> It stays listed under "Your invitation keys" until it expires, is used up or you revoke it. Leaving this page does not delete it. Only the secret key text cannot be shown again, so copy it first.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/invitations" data-invitation-done>Done</a></p>
  <p><strong>Invitation key "build-farm" created.</strong> It is reusable, kind private, and expires: 2026-11-16 08:30 UTC.</p>
  <p>A Worker that enrolls with this key waits for your approval (Workers page) before it receives any operation.</p>
  <p><strong>Copy it now. It is shown only once and cannot be shown again.</strong> If you lose it, revoke it and create a new one.</p>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="invite-key">Invitation key</label>
    <div><div class="copy-field copy-field-wide"><textarea class="copy-value copy-wrap" id="invite-key" rows="1" readonly autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">mnk_9f2c1ab7.m5xwy3dpnz2g65tfobqxgzljnrswc43foj2xizlsmvzwk5dm</textarea><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="#invite-key" data-copy-target="#invite-key" aria-label="Copy the key" title="Copy"><svg class="icon copy-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon copy-check" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" hidden><use href="#i-check"/></svg></button></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Start a Worker with one command</h3>
  <p class="muted">Run this on the machine that should become a Worker. The key is visible in the process list while the command runs; use the file variant below on shared machines.</p>
  <div><div class="copy-field"><pre class="copy-value" id="invite-oneliner">minion worker up --server https://hub.example.com --invite-key mnk_9f2c1ab7.m5xwy3dpnz2g65tfobqxgzljnrswc43foj2xizlsmvzwk5dm</pre><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="#invite-oneliner" data-copy-target="#invite-oneliner" aria-label="Copy the command" title="Copy"><svg class="icon copy-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon copy-check" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" hidden><use href="#i-check"/></svg></button></div></div>
  <h3>Same, with the key in a file</h3>
  <div><div class="copy-field"><pre class="copy-value" id="invite-file">(
  umask 077 &amp;&amp;
  dir=$(mktemp -d &#34;${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/minion-invite.XXXXXX&#34;) &amp;&amp;
  trap &#39;rm -rf &#34;$dir&#34;&#39; EXIT &amp;&amp;
  cat &gt; &#34;$dir/invite.key&#34; &lt;&lt;&#39;EOF&#39; &amp;&amp;
mnk_9f2c1ab7.m5xwy3dpnz2g65tfobqxgzljnrswc43foj2xizlsmvzwk5dm
EOF
  minion worker up --server https://hub.example.com --invite-key &#34;$dir/invite.key&#34;
)
</pre><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="#invite-file" data-copy-target="#invite-file" aria-label="Copy the commands" title="Copy"><svg class="icon copy-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon copy-check" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" hidden><use href="#i-check"/></svg></button></div></div>
  <h3>Docker Compose</h3>
  <p class="muted">A complete Compose project that needs only Docker, <code>bootstrap.sh</code> from the release and the key in a file. The key stays in a secret file; the container reads it through <code>MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE</code>.</p>
  <div><div class="copy-field"><pre class="copy-value" id="invite-compose"># A Minion Worker in Docker, started from the invitation key. Before you start:
# 1. Put bootstrap.sh next to this file. It is a file of the Minion release:
#    https://github.com/patrick-1984/ai-minion/releases/latest/download/bootstrap.sh
# 2. Save the key as the only line of invite_key.txt next to this file.
# 3. Run: MINION_SHARE_EXISTING=later docker compose up -d
#    (the first start needs the sharing choice: all, none or later; later shares nothing
#    until you choose in the Hub. Leave it out on later starts: it replaces the saved choice.)
# 4. Approve the new Worker in the Hub (Workers page): it starts pending and gets no operations until you do.
# The image is built from Alpine with tmux (the Worker drives its sessions through tmux);
# bootstrap.sh downloads and verifies the minion binary on the first start and keeps it in
# the cache volume. The Worker runs as user 10001:10001 and enrolls once: after that the key
# is not needed, but KEEP the file invite_key.txt: Docker needs the mounted file to exist
# whenever the container is restarted or recreated, and the Worker reads it on every start.
# An empty file is safe (an enrolled Worker ignores the key), a missing one stops the start.
# After enrollment erase the secret in place. The init service made the file belong to user
# 10001:10001 (mode 600), so your own shell may not write to it; let the root init service do it:
#    docker compose run --rm --no-deps init sh -c &#39;: &gt; /invite_key.txt&#39;
# That truncates the same file (do not delete, move or replace it with an editor). To remove
# the file itself instead, first remove invite_key.txt from init&#39;s volumes, the secret and
# MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE, then run: docker compose up -d --remove-orphans
services:
  init:
    image: alpine:3.22
    user: &#34;0:0&#34;
    command: [&#34;sh&#34;, &#34;-c&#34;, &#34;chown -R 10001:10001 /data /cache &amp;&amp; chown 10001:10001 /invite_key.txt &amp;&amp; chmod 600 /invite_key.txt&#34;]
    volumes:
      - ./worker-data:/data
      - minion-cache:/cache
      - ./invite_key.txt:/invite_key.txt
  minion-worker:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile_inline: |
        FROM alpine:3.22
        RUN apk add --no-cache tmux
    user: &#34;10001:10001&#34;
    depends_on:
      init:
        condition: service_completed_successfully
    restart: unless-stopped
    entrypoint: [&#34;/bin/sh&#34;, &#34;/bootstrap.sh&#34;]
    command: [&#34;worker&#34;, &#34;up&#34;]
    environment:
      MINION_VERSION: ${MINION_VERSION:-latest}
      MINION_CACHE_DIR: /cache
      MINION_STATE_DIR: /data
      MINION_SHARE_EXISTING: ${MINION_SHARE_EXISTING:-}
      MINION_SERVER: &#34;https://hub.example.com&#34;
      MINION_INVITE_KEY_FILE: /run/secrets/minion_invite_key
    volumes:
      - ./bootstrap.sh:/bootstrap.sh:ro
      - ./worker-data:/data
      - minion-cache:/cache
    secrets:
      - minion_invite_key
secrets:
  minion_invite_key:
    file: ./invite_key.txt
volumes:
  minion-cache:
</pre><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="#invite-compose" data-copy-target="#invite-compose" aria-label="Copy the Compose file" title="Copy"><svg class="icon copy-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon copy-check" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" hidden><use href="#i-check"/></svg></button></div></div>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/invitations" data-invitation-done>Done</a></p>
</div>
